    "lawCode": "Amd §343-k, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S213\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to the \"Upper Hudson Wine\nTrail\"\n\n PURPOSE OF THE BILL :\n\nTo designate the \"Upper Hudson Wine Trail\" within the \"Upper Hudson\nAmerican Viticultural Area\" in order to promote regional agriculture.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 amends the section heading of section 343-k of the highway\nlaw by adding a new subdivision 11, designating portions of the state\nhighway system as the \"Upper Hudson Wine Trail.\" Subdivision 11\nestablishes the routes for the \"Upper Hudson Wine Trail\" which shall\ninclude an east and a west trail.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nWine trails are excellent parts of the agri-tourism market, generating\nincreased room nights and dollars for local economies. The Upper\nHudson region is an area of growth and opportunity for both\nestablished and emerging vineyards and wineries, and the unique\nagricultural characteristics of the region allow for a federal\nAmerican Viticultural Area (AVA) designation. This designation\nidentifies certain regions with distinctive grape-growing climates and\nenvironments in order to enhance the legitimacy of the grapes grown in\nthat region.\n\nTo establish a standard that will promote regional agriculture, the\n\"Upper Hudson Wine Trail Association\" will require that 60% of the\nwine sold in prospective and current member wineries' Wine Tasting &\nSales Rooms consist of grapes and/or fruit grown, processed, and\nbottled in the \"Upper Hudson AVA.\"\n\nEstablishing the \"Upper Hudson Wine Trail\" within the \"Upper Hudson\nAVA\" will encourage increased consumer awareness of this region's wine\nand grape industry and facilitate the development of an \"Upper Hudson\"\nbrand that local residents and tourists alike can recognize and enjoy.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2015-16: Passed Senate\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
