    "lawCode": "Amd §343-k, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S213A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the highway law, in relation to the\n\"Upper Hudson Wine Trail\"\n\n PURPOSE OF THE BILL:\n\nTo promote the New York grape, grape juice and wine industry which\ngenerates more than $4.8 billion in economic benefits annually for New\nYork State. The industry consists of approximately 1,630 family\nvineyards and over 400 wineries which produce 175,000,000 bottles of\nwine, generating $408 million in state and local taxes each year.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the section heading of section 343-k of the highway\nlaw by adding a new subdivision 11, designating portions of the state\nhighway system as the \"Upper Hudson Wine Trail.\"\n\nSubdivision 11 establishes the routes for the \"Upper Hudson Wine\nTrail\" which shall include an east and a west trail.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThere has been a great effort in establishing successful wineries and\nvineyards in the communities of the Saratoga and Capitol Regions. As\nhas been evidenced by many other regions, state designation of a wine\ntrail for tourism and industry promotion is a catalyst for the\nsustainability and profitability of grapes and grape products.\n\nThis trail will highlight the products of this regions fertile glacial\nsoil and ideal grape-growing micro-climates by maximizing the benefits\nof New York State's agricultural and natural resources.\n\nA viable and strong agricultural industry is not only beneficial to\nthe state's farm and food industry, but to the economy of the state,\nhundreds of local communities, and to all consumers of New York.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2015-16: S.8052 - Passed Senate\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nImmediately.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
